Usage: worktree list [--repo PATH] [--no-sync] [--page N] [--limit N]

List registered worktree directories for the resolved repo identity. --repo defaults to the current working directory; the value is canonicalised through `git rev-parse --git-common-dir` so the same physical repository yields the same identity from a main checkout, a linked worktree, or a subdirectory. Returns `{items,page,limit,total_count,has_more,repo_identity}` with page 1 and limit 50 by default. Each item carries directory_id, repo_identity, checkout_path, worktree_path, branch, created_at, tasks, legacy_issues, and sessions. --page is positive and 1-based; --limit is 1..100. An out-of-range page is empty and retains the exact total. The read never creates, migrates, or writes a store or lock file. Available to orchestrator, executor, and reviewer. Authorized Operator/orchestrator callers run a complete repository-scoped `issue sync` before listing and forward its warnings to stderr; --no-sync skips it. Pagination does not limit that sync pass. See docs/cli-pagination.md and docs/worktree-maintenance.md.
